WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
You want to make something good, quickly and have it come out right.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:22.075
Lolly is built for exactly that: fill in a few fields, get a finished file - the layout, the type, the rules are enforced by the tool, not by your eye «unless you want to - then you have a media powerhouse at your fingertips».

00:00:22.425 --> 00:00:26.100
No design software, no waiting.

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:31.025
It runs on your own device and works offline.

00:00:31.771 --> 00:00:34.529
What's in it for you: you ship in minutes

00:00:34.587 --> 00:00:37.394
and it looks like you spent hours.

00:00:38.185 --> 00:00:41.206
You're never stuck waiting on a designer,

00:00:41.278 --> 00:00:44.191
and because the brand rules are baked in,

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.585
it's never your name on the off-brand

00:00:46.647 --> 00:00:47.769
asset.

00:00:48.561 --> 00:00:52.269
You just look fast, polished and reliable.

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:55.870
This page tells you everything you need to

00:00:55.931 --> 00:00:59.119
know about getting the most out of Lolly.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.000
You're one hand in a relay.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:20.800
The tools you author don't stop with you - a developer can wire them into an automated pipeline «Lolly for Builders» and a non-designer colleague can run them self-serve to get a finished, on-brand file without you in the loop.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:27.400
See how the whole lifecycle compounds in The lifecycle of a campaign.

00:01:28.508 --> 00:01:31.394
Why Lolly - your advantages

00:01:32.352 --> 00:01:34.468
Finished, not fiddly.

00:01:35.233 --> 00:01:37.743
The tool already knows the fonts, the

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:40.594
colours, the logo, the spacing.

00:01:41.373 --> 00:01:44.019
You bring the words; it hands back the

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:45.170
asset.

00:01:45.984 --> 00:01:48.668
Nothing to second-guess.

00:01:49.441 --> 00:01:51.968
Correct by construction.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:55.759
Design rules, layout constraints and

00:01:55.822 --> 00:01:58.225
running logic live in the template -

00:01:58.297 --> 00:02:01.573
output can't drift from spec unless the

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:03.666
tool's author deliberately leaves

00:02:03.729 --> 00:02:05.369
something open.

00:02:06.158 --> 00:02:09.526
Wild creative range, inside guard-rails

00:02:09.585 --> 00:02:10.894
that hold.

00:02:11.682 --> 00:02:14.444
One source, every format.

00:02:15.216 --> 00:02:18.371
The same design exports as SVG,

00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:22.910
print-ready PDF, high-res PNG, or 60fps

00:02:22.972 --> 00:02:24.069
video.

00:02:24.855 --> 00:02:27.844
Make it once; ship it everywhere.

00:02:28.628 --> 00:02:31.393
Infinite permutations.

00:02:32.186 --> 00:02:35.540
Localise a card into a dozen languages,

00:02:35.607 --> 00:02:39.028
generate every size for every placement,

00:02:39.118 --> 00:02:42.256
swap a lockup across forty campaigns - all

00:02:42.341 --> 00:02:46.194
from one design, driven by a spreadsheet.

00:02:46.575 --> 00:02:50.000
It's yours, offline, private.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:03:00.250
Your work stays on your device - no account needed, nothing uploaded to make or export an asset, no licence to audit.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:05.200
Close the laptop lid on a plane and keep working.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:12.475
«Two optional server add-ons exist and can be ignored entirely - see Server Surface.»

00:03:13.215 --> 00:03:15.594
Open, not locked in.

00:03:16.373 --> 00:03:19.430
The engine is open source and your work

00:03:19.492 --> 00:03:22.538
lives at plain URL'S, not inside a

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:24.444
vendor's database.

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:28.069
Superpowers when you want them.

00:03:28.832 --> 00:03:31.440
You never have to design - but the moment

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:34.695
you decide to, the ceiling is high.

00:03:35.479 --> 00:03:38.361
Lay out pages freehand on the Design

00:03:38.422 --> 00:03:39.644
canvas.

00:03:40.406 --> 00:03:43.364
Cut clips, cards and music on a timeline

00:03:43.399 --> 00:03:45.444
in Sequence Studio.

00:03:46.229 --> 00:03:49.243
Record clean voice and camera takes with

00:03:49.307 --> 00:03:50.944
live coaching.

00:03:51.724 --> 00:03:55.213
Stand up an entire brand yourself, guided

00:03:55.274 --> 00:03:57.748
by a colour picker that tells you more

00:03:57.805 --> 00:04:00.476
about a colour than most design suites

00:04:00.565 --> 00:04:01.869
ever will.

00:04:02.636 --> 00:04:05.047
The constraints don't cage you - they

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:06.494
catch you.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:10.371
Think of the guard-rails as bumper lanes:

00:04:10.433 --> 00:04:13.065
you still throw the ball - the words, the

00:04:13.141 --> 00:04:16.371
image, the idea - and the code just keeps

00:04:16.426 --> 00:04:18.976
it out of the gutter so it can never break

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:20.344
the brand.

00:04:21.135 --> 00:04:23.636
You're not being automated away; the

00:04:23.728 --> 00:04:26.825
tedious part is: the brand-checking, the

00:04:26.904 --> 00:04:29.182
re-exporting at every size, the

00:04:29.243 --> 00:04:32.645
hand-localizing into a dozen languages.

00:04:33.433 --> 00:04:37.118
What's left is the call that needed you.

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:40.797
And the tool you author is what lets the

00:04:40.866 --> 00:04:43.558
rest of the company make good work without

00:04:43.621 --> 00:04:46.242
pulling you into every asset: your

00:04:46.303 --> 00:04:48.194
judgment, scaled.

00:04:49.346 --> 00:04:51.372
How it compares

00:04:52.402 --> 00:04:56.368
Lolly isn't trying to be Canva or Figma.

00:04:57.126 --> 00:05:00.417
It sits where rules, repeatability and

00:05:00.478 --> 00:05:03.215
hard constraints matter more than freehand

00:05:03.297 --> 00:05:06.295
flexibility - turning design decisions

00:05:06.384 --> 00:05:09.532
into tools your whole team can use without

00:05:09.623 --> 00:05:12.619
you in the loop for every asset.

00:05:13.391 --> 00:05:16.028
The product-by-product detail lives on the

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:20.085
dated comparison pages - Canva, Adobe,

00:05:20.175 --> 00:05:24.242
Figma, Penpot, brand portals, render APIs

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:27.526
and file converters - with the concessions

00:05:27.588 --> 00:05:30.315
written first and a capability board

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:31.769
behind them.

00:05:32.545 --> 00:05:34.976
Reach for Lolly for the assets you make

00:05:35.017 --> 00:05:37.993
again and again - event signage, quote

00:05:38.056 --> 00:05:40.576
cards, localized banners, email

00:05:40.657 --> 00:05:42.984
signatures, shipping labels, social

00:05:43.045 --> 00:05:46.244
variants, data-driven charts and maps.

00:05:47.027 --> 00:05:50.006
Reach for a design tool for the bespoke

00:05:50.068 --> 00:05:53.650
hero piece, the one-off campaign concept,

00:05:53.712 --> 00:05:56.347
the ideation that's meant to escape the

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:57.594
system.

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:01.309
Lolly executes the system; it doesn't

00:06:01.353 --> 00:06:03.494
replace the studio.

00:06:04.638 --> 00:06:06.600
What you can make

00:06:07.937 --> 00:06:10.839
Everything correct, without the wait

00:06:11.813 --> 00:06:14.341
Fill in a few fields, get the finished

00:06:14.425 --> 00:06:17.453
asset - no fonts to pick, no colours to

00:06:17.524 --> 00:06:20.720
second-guess, no "is this the right logo?"

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:24.143
The tool already knows.

00:06:24.913 --> 00:06:28.200
Email signatures, event countdowns, quote

00:06:28.262 --> 00:06:31.255
cards, badges, street maps - everything

00:06:31.316 --> 00:06:34.301
your team needs on a Tuesday at 4pm,

00:06:34.367 --> 00:06:35.844
self-serve.

00:06:36.613 --> 00:06:39.258
And because no customer data leaves the

00:06:39.318 --> 00:06:42.397
device, there's no compliance risk to

00:06:42.457 --> 00:06:43.995
collaborating.

00:06:44.775 --> 00:06:48.187
Street Map is a fair example of the trade:

00:06:48.254 --> 00:06:51.335
you pick a city and a couple of colours,

00:06:51.396 --> 00:06:53.982
and the cartography, the road weights and

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:56.844
the water are decided for you.

00:06:57.974 --> 00:07:01.221
From live data to finished visual

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:06.489
Connect a CSV or JSON table to a chart,

00:07:06.562 --> 00:07:09.382
map, or table template and update the

00:07:09.444 --> 00:07:12.795
numbers - the layout takes care of itself.

00:07:13.569 --> 00:07:15.910
Election results, quarterly earnings,

00:07:15.969 --> 00:07:18.926
weather events: build the format once and

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:22.269
reuse it every time the story runs.

00:07:23.052 --> 00:07:25.853
Match your house style exactly, because

00:07:25.944 --> 00:07:28.551
it's enforced at the template level, not

00:07:28.613 --> 00:07:31.044
left as a loose guideline.

00:07:32.171 --> 00:07:34.819
Tools that compose tools

00:07:35.771 --> 00:07:38.203
One tool can embed another tool's live

00:07:38.265 --> 00:07:41.835
output as an asset - a name badge that

00:07:41.899 --> 00:07:45.849
renders its own QR code, a card that drops

00:07:45.881 --> 00:07:48.775
in a live chart - with no design tool and

00:07:48.835 --> 00:07:51.020
no manual compositing.

00:07:51.784 --> 00:07:54.037
The embedded render stays live and

00:07:54.097 --> 00:07:57.196
re-renders on load; it's never a flattened

00:07:57.256 --> 00:07:58.395
picture.

00:07:59.527 --> 00:08:02.233
The frontier, when you need it

00:08:03.183 --> 00:08:06.643
Advanced filters, compositing, animation,

00:08:06.705 --> 00:08:09.800
live camera effects, generative design -

00:08:09.873 --> 00:08:12.691
every web technology is available to a

00:08:12.752 --> 00:08:16.545
template author, so the ceiling is high.

00:08:17.323 --> 00:08:20.656
Author tools, not files: build the thing

00:08:20.715 --> 00:08:23.613
that generates 10000 cards rather than

00:08:23.665 --> 00:08:26.243
making 10000 cards.

00:08:27.024 --> 00:08:29.931
Lock what shouldn't change; expose only

00:08:29.994 --> 00:08:32.094
what's meant to vary.

00:08:33.217 --> 00:08:35.595
Touches you'll notice

00:08:36.175 --> 00:08:38.625
Print, done right.

00:08:38.975 --> 00:08:54.325
Real physical units «mm/cm/in/pt» and DPI, bleed and crop marks, CMYK and PDF/X-4 output-intent - a print shop gets exactly what it needs.

00:08:54.675 --> 00:08:57.000
See Exporting.

00:08:57.350 --> 00:09:00.125
Video and motion.

00:09:00.475 --> 00:09:13.600
Export WebM/MP4 «with audio tracks», animated PNG/WebP and animated SVG - from the same template that makes your stills.

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:36.325
Sequence Studio goes further: a real timeline under the canvas, with a magnetic row of clips, free overlay lanes, trim and split, transition presets, voiceover recording and a music mix - rendered out as MP4, WebM, GIF or APNG by a deterministic compositor rather than a screen recording.

00:09:36.675 --> 00:09:43.250
Lottie files come in as animated assets and render out to any of those.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:54.150
Above the clips sit keyframes: pose a box at one instant, lift it off the page with real depth and fly a camera over the result.

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:59.525
See Using Lolly → Timeline and Animating.

00:09:59.875 --> 00:10:01.700
Audio.

00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:20.500
Record a voice note and save it as MP3 «or its native M4A/OGG/WebM», all on-device - and bring in MP3, WAV, OGG, M4A, FLAC, MIDI or tracker modules «MOD/XM/IT/…»

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:27.425
as a music bed under a video or an ambient track in Neurospicy Mode.

00:10:28.165 --> 00:10:30.219
Draw, don't settle.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:34.281
The Design tool has a real pen: click to

00:10:34.342 --> 00:10:37.159
place points, drag to curve and pick the

00:10:37.221 --> 00:10:39.894
kind of curve that runs through them.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.288
Combine shapes with union, subtract,

00:10:43.332 --> 00:10:46.716
intersect and exclude, outline a stroke,

00:10:46.779 --> 00:10:50.015
offset a silhouette, simplify a path - the

00:10:50.076 --> 00:10:53.965
geometry is exact Bezier maths, so a shape

00:10:54.022 --> 00:10:56.526
you draw stays crisp at any size and

00:10:56.587 --> 00:10:59.173
renders identically from a link or the

00:10:59.241 --> 00:11:00.394
CLI.

00:11:01.185 --> 00:11:05.269
See Using Lolly → Drawing your own shapes.

00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:08.325
Editable vectors.

00:11:08.675 --> 00:11:13.225
SVG, EPS, EMF and DXF export.

00:11:13.575 --> 00:11:23.400
Text becomes outlined paths in vector output, so a print shop or a cutter gets crisp geometry that opens anywhere.

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:33.075
«Outlined text is no longer re-typable in Illustrator - that's the trade for perfect fidelity without the font.»

00:11:33.814 --> 00:11:36.568
Convenience that adds up.

00:11:37.338 --> 00:11:39.766
Batch a spreadsheet into a folder of

00:11:39.842 --> 00:11:43.167
assets; save sessions and organise them

00:11:43.202 --> 00:11:47.171
into Projects; share any state as a URL;

00:11:47.242 --> 00:11:50.294
render a whole folder as one zip.

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:54.343
A UI that's actually pleasant.

00:11:55.133 --> 00:11:58.445
Undo/redo everywhere, a sound layer you

00:11:58.504 --> 00:12:01.904
can turn off, a theme cycle, live-camera

00:12:01.999 --> 00:12:04.586
filters - and Neurospicy Mode, a

00:12:04.648 --> 00:12:07.304
background focus-music player that follows

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:10.344
you across the app in its own dock.

00:12:11.106 --> 00:12:14.519
A calmer interface when you want one.

00:12:15.305 --> 00:12:17.978
Four switches under Profile →

00:12:18.058 --> 00:12:20.930
Accessibility - Reduce motion, Hide

00:12:21.017 --> 00:12:23.896
colourful previews, High contrast and

00:12:23.957 --> 00:12:26.427
Large text - settle the app around your

00:12:26.488 --> 00:12:27.494
work.

00:12:28.262 --> 00:12:31.367
Each is off until you turn it on, and none

00:12:31.409 --> 00:12:34.644
of them touch your canvas or move a pixel

00:12:34.711 --> 00:12:36.719
of what you export.

00:12:37.525 --> 00:12:41.518
See Your profile → Accessibility.

00:12:42.654 --> 00:12:45.115
Get the most out of it

00:12:46.075 --> 00:12:49.418
Quickstart - brand in, first file out.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:56.500
The Brand Studio - shape your logos, colours, type and tokens «#/start».

